        "subject": "LU-18687 llite: remove SLAB_MEM_SPREAD entirely",
        "message": "LU-18687 llite: remove SLAB_MEM_SPREAD entirely\n\nSLAB_MEM_SPREAD only ever had an effect with CONFIG_SLAB, where\nit enabled cpuset memory spreading in alternate_node_alloc();\nSLUB always ignored it. No supported distro kernel was built\nwith CONFIG_SLAB (RHEL and Ubuntu have shipped SLUB throughout),\nand the SLAB allocator itself was removed in kernel v6.8. The\nflag was deprecated to zero in v6.9 and removed in v6.10, with\nall in-kernel users dropped.\n\nRemove the last user in super25.c and the compat definition,\nmatching the upstream kernel-wide cleanup. No functional change.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ie98fdbe5fe65854ded34b45490c6896e6a6a6964\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/67947\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
